      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-12-13_WidnesExaminer_art0130" n="art0130">
        <head>Caretakers' Wages.</head>
        <p>Caretakers' Wages.</p>
        <p>The Education Committee report a petition from the Caretakers' Association re the wages of the school caretakers, and a deputation is to be received representing the association.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-12-13_WidnesExaminer_art0131" n="art0131">
        <head>Infirmary Ball.</head>
        <p>The Infirmary Ball.</p>
        <p>One of the most attractive balls of the festive season is that known as the Infirmary Ball. It will take place at Parr Hall on 19th January. bancers should book up the date for this ball.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-12-13_WidnesExaminer_art0132" n="art0132">
        <head>Gift to Infirmary.</head>
        <p>Gift to Infirmary.</p>
        <p>The Matron of the Infirmary acknowledges the receipt of 14 articles of clothing from the Warrington Needlework Guild.</p>
        <p>Warrington Market Prices.</p>
        <p>The prices on Wednesday were: Wheat. 4s. 4d. to 4s. 6d. per 70th.; oats, 2s. 6d. to 25. Bd. per 451 h.; wheat straw, 295. per ton; oat straw, 295. to 31s. per ton: XX flour, 235. 3(1. per 2401 b.; bran, is. per 20113.</p>
