        <p>COLTNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. EDUCATION COMMITTEE. TO BUILDERS AND CONTRACTORS. The SITES and BUILDINGS COMMITTEE is prepared to receive - TENDERS for the ERECTION of a PUBLIC ELEMENTARY SCHOOL, to by known as the Oakwood Avenue Council Sclool. Bills of Quantities and Instructions to Builders and Contractors may be obtained on and after the 22nd December from the Educa- tion Office on payment of One Guinea, which will be returned upon the receipt of a bona-fide tender. The Tenders must be delivered at the Educa- tion Office in the envelope supplied (which must be securely sealed with wax) by not later than 12 o'clock noon on Friday, the 16th January, 1914. The Committee does not bind itself to accept the lowest or any Tender. J. MOORE MURRAY, -M.Sc., Secretary and Director. Edneotion Offic.e, Warrington, 10th December, 1913.</p>
