        <p>--- W A.R RINGTON UNION. HANDYMAN REQUIRED. The Guardians invite applications for the Appointment of HANDYMAN at the Cottage Homes and Schools. Padgate, near Warrington. Salary, 28s. per week. rising at the end of one year's satisfactory service to 30s. per week (non- resident). Particulars as to duties may be obtained upon application to the Superintendent of the Homes. Applications to be made upon forms to ~.be obtained from me, the undersigned. and must , he returned, duly comnletNL not later than 10 a.m. on Monda.v, the 29th December. 1913. Canvassing the Guardians directly or in- directly' will disqualify. By order. ARTHUR BOTTOMLEY, Clerk. -Union Offices. Bewsey Chambers, Warrington, 6th December, 1913.</p>
        <p>LOW- PRICED COKE. THE Warrington Corporation Gas Department , have decided to retail COKE in half-cwt. lots. Coke is the cheapest fuel, and if used instead Of coal would effect great economy and diminish Hinoke. , The Gas Department deliver Coke in cart loads 10 any customer, or in bags to several customers 'II the same street at small extra cost. Write Longford Gas Works. Telephone No. 4. NVARRINGIAMILEngerr'S COLLEGE, TIIE ANNUAL CONCERT Will be held in PARR HALL, On THURSDAY, DECEMBER 18th, 1913. MISCELLANEOUS PROGRAMME. Reserved chairs (centre gallery), 2s. Reserved chairs (body of hall), Is. Gd. Reserved Seats (side gallery, front row only), 8. 6d. Unreserved, is., and 6d. Children half-price to all parts. T• ickets may be obtained from Teachers and ocholars. uPlan of Reserved Seats at R. H. Pearson's, ridge-street, Wednesday. December 3rd, at 9 a.m. open at 6.45. Concert 7.30 prompt.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. The Health Committee require the services of TWO LADY INSPECTORS, who shall act as Health Visitors, and, if required, as Inspectors of Midwives. Candidates must hold certificate for at least three years' training as Nurse in a General Hos- pital. and must also possess the certificate of the Central Midwives Board.. Preference will be given to candidates who have had nursing • experience among children, and hold the Health Visitor's Certificate, or the Sanitary Inspector's Certificate. Salary XBO per annum, rising by annual in- crements of £5 to a maximum of £lOO. „t 5 annual allowance for uniform. Applications to be made on forms to be obtained- from this office, together with copies of not more than three testimonials, to be sent in to the undersigned not later than Saturday, December 20th, 1913, and endorsed "Health Visitor." G, W. N. JOSEPH, Medical Officer of Health. Health Department, 78, Sankey-street, Warrington.</p>
